  tokyo to further strengthen  our eu japan relationship i thank you  thank you mr president and now i pass  the flow to the president of the  european commission thank you very much  good morning  indeed we had a very productive eu  japan summit japan is  a like-minded partner of the european  union and we have made  good progress on our partnership there  is still a lot to be done  but we went through each of the topics  and there's a lot of cooperation that we  are working on to increase  the the common agenda indeed the first  point on our common agenda was climate  the  the fight against climate change and  here  japan is one of the first countries that  has committed  to climate neutrality in 2050 it was  last fall  so they are like the european union very  committed  to the long-term goals i very much  welcome that  it will be interesting to see the goal  defined by japan by 2030  and we want to work very uh much we want  to work  much closer on this topic together  that's why we indeed started the first  ever  green alliance with japan and there's a  whole agenda that is in this green agile  alliance um in the green transition  we want to inspire others to join of  course and therefore this clean alliance  is also so important in the run up  to the cup 15 on biodiversity in kunming  and the cup 26 on climate in glasgow  because we  really need to move to to form this  movement  towards tangible reliable goals  we put for ourselves out there to fight  climate change  and to fight the loss of biodiversity  there are few topics or examples of the  green alliance  for example that we shape global  standards or that we  both push forward sustainable finance  like green bonds  and that we are firm on carbon pricing  but we also see  an enormous potential in cooperating in  the green alliance  for example on clean energy we will be  signing a memorandum of cooperation  on hydrogen with japan in the second  half of these years  this paves the way but  there are also other topics like the  offshore wind  to work there closely together all this  was part of our  of our discussions in this summit  on bilateral trade another topic here  the cornerstone is the economic  partnership agreement  it has joined priority and we have to  implement it fully  we will focus on delivering concrete  benefits  in non-tariff areas and on clarifying  the free flow of data under our  agreement for instance  and uh we will continue working on  market  access within this economic partnership  agreement  for eu agricultural products and on the  remaining sanitary and phyto-sanitary  issues  that have to be resolved on multilateral  trade  we share absolutely the views on the  necessity to reform wto  and as we're very happy that the  u.s with president biden is back at the  negotiation table  we should now use the momentum mainly to  develop new multilateral rules  and to unlock the dispute settlement  mechanism  here we agreed that we will push  together  for really having a concrete result in  the ministerial conference  of wto in the second half of the year  on digital japan is our oldest and  closest partner  in the digital field and once more  here too we share the same vision  of human-centric digitization  so we want to build a partnership for  the digital decade with japan  we are investing in connectivity  we can work together on standards for  example  on the ethical use of artificial  intelligence  we will promote as i've said the digital  trade flows through resilient supply  chains and secure  cyberspace just to name a few examples  of this potential  and fifth on my last point  we also discussed the global fight  against the pandemic  both the european union and japan have  made significant contributions  to covax to ensure access to vaccines  for all  the european union will continue to  support the efforts to fight the  pandemic  including exporting vaccines  here there was a very clear question  from our japanese partners  it is a sign of solidarity and a sign of  friendship with japan  that so far the european union has  authorized  more than 100 million doses to be  exported  to japan that is approximately enough to  vaccinate  40 percent of the population and this  reflects  the very strong bonds between the  european union and japan thanks a lot  thank you madam president let me simply  highlight um  that the eu japan green alliance and the  ambitious  joint statement on eu and japan was  published  just now on our website and we're going  to turn to the q  a session now please can i ask you to um  to put your cameras on and raise your  yellow hand it is now  just minding you that we have japanese  translation as well and we have the  first question from associated press by  samuel  petrikin samuel you have the floor  [Music]  [Music]  [Music]  [Music]  [Music]  [Music]  yes little to act uh i think  indeed we have of course said that we're  looking forward to the olympic games  no more has been discussed but uh the  signal that  from the european union uh 100 more than  100 million doses of vaccines have been  authorized to be exported to japan  also is a strong sign that we support  any preparation for the olympic games  games and the safety  of these games thank you  turning to stuart lau now from politico  stewart um hi  thank you i'd just like to ask more  specifically about  the issues of the east china sea and the  south china sea that you discussed with  the japanese side because  um would like to know more about what  exactly was discussed  and second of all i mean on taiwan the  japanese prime minister when he was in  washington  they shat light on the issue of taiwan  did the issue come up at all  during today's um summit thank you  yes indeed the maritime security is a  top priority and  and we think with japan we are convinced  with japan  this is very important to cooperate you  know to make sure that we can improve  the maritime security uh everywhere but  also in this part i